Z||000003||ThatRickGuy||01-04-2001||08:51 AM||||I think it's maters on the cop, I got a ticket for going 75 in the 65 area of I-95 at 3 in the morning in the '76 Lemans, but I got a warning from a cop who followed me for 3 miles while I was doing 80 in a 55 on I-95 at 1:30am in my Fiero. who knows, but maybe it's time to move to a new county, just to avoid that cop. or you could plead harasment at your court case...||||reg||1
Z||000004||fiero56||01-04-2001||09:00 AM||||I was given more crap back when I had my '88 Sable than I have ever gotten in my Fiero. Almost every day cops would literally follow me everywhere, through dubdivisions, parking lots, etc. When I drove my Fiero they acted like they never even saw me. Now I just have the Fieros, and cops still never even take a second look. ||||reg||1
Z||000005||overlord||01-04-2001||09:08 AM||||ya..the cops around here dont like my fiero either! ALthohg i havent got any speeding tickets or anything like that...yet.<BR>Lets see,  cop pulls me over and says i have to take my window tint off, "sure thing" i say.  2 days later the same cop pulls me over and gives me a ticket for having the window tint on. I explained to him how it takes a little time and effort to get it off and that i work nights and sleep all day, its kinda hard to do until i get a night off of work....Think he cares?  nope.<P>Another time i was on the highway and a cop went by me, as i was watching my rear view mirror, sure enogh he uballs it and starts following me...Now i was at a part  of the road where it goes down a valley and is very easy to exceed the speed limit.  So i kept the speedo at exactly 100 kph (and i mean EXACTLY) down the valley and then back up..Sure enogh, as soon as im back on straight highway, the cop turns around.<P>So why would a cop turn his car around, follow me for miles?, when i am not exceeding the limit, had my belt on, even had my lights on for safety. <P>||||reg||1
Z||000006||1FieroGTRacingInc||01-04-2001||09:16 AM||||I get pulled over ALL the time(7 times so far) by the same cop for...........  no front plate....  what a hooot!!  all warning ticket's.<P>------------------<BR>1FieroGTRacingInc.||||reg||1
Z||000007||stimpy||01-04-2001||09:33 AM||||Usually I am respectful to the cops that pull me over, but I think if a cop went down on his knees to start smelling my seat covers, I would lose all self control and laugh my ass off! He'd smell the aftermath of green leafy vegitation alright, but it would be broccoli, not ganja!||||reg||1
Z||000008||Oreif||01-04-2001||10:02 AM||||Around here the police pull over riced out cars more than Fiero's. I ususally get stopped when I get a different car. I work nights and I think they are out looking for drunks. I usually get pulled over for something lame like 45 in a 40. Once I tell them I'm coming home from work, they "let me off with a warning" and I don't get stopped again. It's like if they see the same person in the same car every night they remember who I am and know I'm on my way home from work. As for being polite, Most around here are straight forward and don't give a lot of B.S. or snide comments. (well to me anyway)||||reg||1
Z||000009||Raydar||01-04-2001||10:58 AM||||Jake, <BR>Sounds like you got on the wrong side of that guy in a hurry. He'll probably screw with you for a while. Just try to convince him that you're not a bad guy. <BR>And <I>be polite.</I> Even if he doesn't deserve it. <BR>If he's not a complete a$$hole, he'll finally decide that you represent no challenge to him, and he'll look for someone else to bother. <BR>And remember, he may not always be right. But he <I>is</I> always the police. <P>||||reg||1
Z||000010||pHoOl||01-04-2001||12:54 PM||||I have a nice story too.<P>Couple of weeks ago, i got together with a female friend of mine who i hadn't seen in a while.  we went out to a coffee shop and then just kinda visited with her mom for a while.  when i started nearing the shopping center that the coffee shop was in so that i could drop her off at her car, i noticed that the same cop passed me twice in two different directions.  Thinking this was odd, i started watching the rear view mirror.  Next i had another cop, different car behind me.  Not liking to have cops tail me, i pulled into the left turn lane to make a turn until he passed me, then pulled back into traffic.  at the next light, i turned left, and he went straight, so i thought i was set.  I pull into the parking lot to drop her off, and we started up another conversation so i turned around and we started driving again.  i took one of the back exit roads out of the shopping center and a mile later got to a stop sign.  I then noticed that there were jeep headlights behind me (that's the same car as the second cop that was behind me).  I turned to her and said "bet ya hundred to one that it's a cop behind us" she turned around and said "yep".<P>So i make my right turn and so does he, and sure enough, the lights come on.  I knew that i wasn't speeding or doing any strange driving, so i had no idea what they could possibly pull me over for.  He gets out of the car and starts asking me if i had been drinking, and my age and such.  I of course wasn't drinking, underage.  He's sitting there checking my license for a few minutes and then another cop car rolls up.  I was wondering what on earth was going on, cause i knew that i didn't do anything.  that cop talks to him for a few minutes, then pulls through.  It couldnt' have been more than five minutes later that i third cop car pulls in, and talks to the first cop.  I was starting to get really irritated.  He hands me back my license and such and says "okay" then starts walking towards his car.<P>Bottom line?  If you're 19, drive an 88 fiero GT, have a personalized license plate, and a backwards hat, you're a suspicious vehicle.  I think that i heard him say that i was a suspicious vehicle too over the radio.  Anybody else think that this sounds kinda like goofy?<P>------------------<BR>AIM: phool88fiero<P>   <IMG SRC="http://www.gvsuphool.homestead.com/files/pHoOl_sig.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000011||Jake||01-04-2001||01:38 PM||||I don't understand how I got on his bad side. He knows who I am. I've never been in trouble with the law for anything except traffic violations. And this is a cop who had saved my ex-girlfriends life. She had gotten into a car accident and he pulled her out of the car (she wasn't breathing) and gave her CPR. Before he let me go the first time, even after everything he tried to get me for...I shook his hand and thanked him for doing that, yet he still showed no kindness. He just says "well I'm gonna tell you right now, don't do that sh!t anymore. Cause I got my eye on you" I mean come on, everyone speeds from time to time. I hardly ever do it. I am a sensible driver 90% of the time. But I do speed every now and then and maybe even a burn-out here and there. But I'm a car guy, I like to feel a little power sometimes  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> What really gets me is how hipocritical he is. I see him speeding all the time. And one time he actually had my friend with him. After they had taken him to the police station and found out he didn't do anything wrong. He put him in the backseat in cuffs and proceeded to drive him home. My friend, just making chit-chat says "So what will these things do?" and to his suprise the cop hammers it! He brought the speedometer up to 110mph through our little small town on the main road where kids cross all the time and what-not. Kinda bothers me. I know I'm only 18 years old, but just cause I'm young doesn't mean I'm a drugaddict...and the fact that he can sit there and lecture someone for their unsafe driving when he does it 3 times as bad. I don't know guys, just had to blow off some steam  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><BR>||||reg||12
Z||000012||sqoach||01-04-2001||02:07 PM||||cops bother me too in my small town. they follow me around a lot. i've got one of the only two fieros in town. i've only been stopped once by them though. and it was something stupid.<P>just cruising along main street like a lot of people do at night. cop starts to follow me for a few blocks, turns on the lights and i pull over of course. i had no idea what it was for. cops comes up to my side and says, "you know you got your fog lamps on?" and i said, "yeah." cops says something like you're not suppose to use them in town and when it's not foggy or raining. i swear i passed two other cars that had them on. i see people with them on all the time and the cops don't stop them.<BR>and what harm does it to to have them on? i have mine pointed down a bit so they don't blind anyone.<BR>stupid cops...<P>------------------<BR>sQoaCh<BR>sqoach@yahoo.com<BR>        <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/mysig_2.JPG"> ||||reg||8
Z||000013||overlord||01-04-2001||05:49 PM||||o ya, i had the fog lights story too.<BR>And i only use them at night when visibility is not perfect. I see people ALL the time with foglights on in the daytime.....and my town is small..i mean small.....1500 people maybe.....so shouldnt every one of those people with their fog lights on have been pulled over too?..........guess not..they arent driving little sports cars.||||reg||1
Z||000014||Raydar||01-04-2001||06:15 PM||||  <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Jake:<BR><B>...And this is a cop who had saved my ex-girlfriends life. She had gotten into a car accident and he pulled her out of the car (she wasn't breathing) and gave her CPR. Before he let me go the first time, even after everything he tried to get me for...I shook his hand and thanked him for doing that, yet he still showed no kindness. He just says "well I'm gonna tell you right now, don't do that sh!t anymore. Cause I got my eye on you" I mean come on, everyone speeds from time to time. I hardly ever do it. I am a sensible driver 90% of the time. But I do speed every now and then and maybe even a burn-out here and there. But I'm a car guy, I like to feel a little power sometimes    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> </B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Maybe he doesn't want to have to give <I>you</I> CPR, anytime soon. I bet that $hit wears on you, after a while. <BR>Of course I understand the need to feel a little horsepower kick you in the back, but if your luck runs like mine does, the first time you do <I>anything</I> wrong in a year, the sucker is gonna be sitting there watching you. He'll never see you, all those times that you <I>aren't</I> goofing off.<BR>And you're right. There is <I>no</I> excuse for him driving 110 through the middle of town. That's irresponsible as hell. <BR>Just be cool and attempt to not cross paths with him. He sounds like a real piece of work.<P>And don't even get me started on fog lights. The morons around here drive around with them on all the time. Blinds the hell out of oncoming traffic. <BR>Makes we want to rig up a light bar on my Sonoma and mount some runway lights on it, to be used just for their benefit. (Yeah, I can be irresponsible, too.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"> ) <p>[This message has been edited by Raydar (edited 01-04-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000015||80's BOY||01-04-2001||06:48 PM||||i was tagged by small-town cops where i'm from too. back in-the-day i had an s-10 blazer and they were so despaerate to look inside, they busted me for spinning my tires at a stoplight. but get this....IT WAS RAINING!!!! $125 fine. man i was pissed. they "detained my for my safety" while they called the drug dog to sniff my ride. i had just walled out the back end with 2 punch 12's and 18's so the vinyl was fresh. they threatened to cut the speakers open if i didn't fess up. idiots! i was just a college kid with a loud stereo. as i was pulled over my redneck buddy rags on his straight pipe exhaust from his dually and they just laugh as he goes by. small town crap sux. ||||reg||8
Z||000016||KnightRyder31||01-04-2001||08:13 PM||||I think most cops hate me!<BR>I am also going to one...HAHAHAHA!<BR>They really didn't like that Bonneville that I had.<P>||||reg||1
Z||000017||Jake||01-04-2001||08:29 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Raydar:<BR><B>  Maybe he doesn't want to have to give <I>you</I> CPR, anytime soon. </B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Maybe not, but he didn't even know who I was untill I told him so I'm not someone special he's trying to keep safe  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"> but yeah, you're right, it probably does wear on ya after a while<BR>||||reg||6
Z||000018||Bigfieroman||01-05-2001||12:25 AM||||I was driving the backroads in our local county park, and I turned onto a road where there is no streetlight etc.  So I couldnt see the tunr and went a little wide.  Well, it attracts the attention of the cop behind me, so he follows me.  (little to my knowlege)  So, all i see are headlights behind me, in the middle of an uninhabited park, so i give it a little gas to pull away.  It go to be quite a street race.  45 Mph on wet roads, bald tires, 15MPH turns.  He nearlylost it, so he gets all "My dick is bigger than yours" on me and pulls me over after 3 miles.  $146 ticket, and said, ohh, ill give you a break on the reckless driving, since the speeding was so much.  clocked me at 42 in a 25, said i peaked at 57.  Jeez...I just hope my insurance doesn't find out.||||reg||1
Z||000019||trigger||01-05-2001||08:13 PM||||I know what you mean.  I got pulled over for taking a turn to sharp coming out of the high school.  He says something about accelerating fast, but he won't worry about because my puny little car won't spin the tires.  Then he's has the nuts to tell me I might want to consider driving school since I just have a school permit.  A few months later my friend is talking to the cop and asks him if he remembers the kid in the red sports car, and he says yeah the cocky little mother f***** deserved everything I gave him and then some.  I was at least five under the speed limit the whole time.  $50 ticket too.  Oh well, I'm done venting for know.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>------------------<BR>Honestly officer, I was just keeping up with the flow of traffic.  I know there aren't any cars in the area, that's how far behind I am.||||reg||1
Z||000020||BigBoyToys||01-05-2001||11:45 PM||||Yeh rite cops don't PROFILE!!!<BR>To keep a long story short. I use to drive 3 miles to work every day (first shift) then I got transfered, now 25 miles each way. Driving a red 88 IROC-Z28 I was now was being stopped for BS about once every three months for about 3 years. <P>Now I change positions at work to a second shift job and my stop rate climbs to an average of 3 times a month (still mostly BS stops). So winter comes and I get a 90 Z24 as a winter car and my stop rate goes to once a month (still mostly BS stops). Spring comes and I get my 86 GT (and also run my IROC on nice nights) stop rate goes back up to an average of 3 stops a month. Winter comes and out comes the Z24 but in December I total the  car (old guy didn't see me). <P>Now the kicker, a buddy at work has a 88 SLAAB 9000 Turbo 4dr, so I pick it up, now go ahead and guess what my stop rate was for over 8 months... thats right ZERO!!! Not once have I been pulled over and I drive the same way at the same speeds over the same route and past the same cops. They never even give me another look. Now I just got a 2000 Silverado and so far 1 month down and no pull.<P>Never plead guilty, Never request a supporting disposition (just pi$$e$ the cop off), Never bring a lawyer (just pi$$e$ off the judge), Never look like you have money (the dirt bags aways get the big breaks, even better is if you can find a dirty little runny nose kid to be holding), always take it to trial, talk to the cop (nicely) they will always plea bargian a lesser infraction. If you don't believe go see for your self, anybody is allowed into traffic court, get a seat up close so you can hear for yourself how justice is handed out by our fine and fair civil servants. <P>Enough said! Sorry for the long post. <P>But if I have not endangered persons or property, have not caused a dangerous situation and my car is inspected, registered and insured I should be able to drive whatever I choose with out concern that I fit police profile and WILL now be subjected to police harassment.<P>And then they have the nerve to call my home solicitating for donations in return for a sticker. I now tell this very story ending with where they can stick that sticker.<P>Peace ||||reg||13
Z||000021||Cheever2||01-06-2001||12:21 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Bigfieroman:<BR>... So, all i see are headlights behind me, in the middle of an uninhabited park, so i give it a little gas to pull away...<HR></BLOCKQUOTE>When I was a teenager, going to work one night, I once had a pair of headlights right on my back bumper.  No other cars on a lonely road in the middle of the night, and I hadn't done anything wrong.  I thought I can either slam on the brakes then get out and slam on his teeth, or I can just try to pull away.  I chose the less confrontational method, and discovered like you that it was a cop who needed to make his quota.  Next time I will slam on the brakes and say there was a kid or a dog running out onto the road in front of me.  Sorry, My7fieros, but I KNOW you have quotas.  I dated a cop's daughter and she told me. <P><BR>||||reg||6
Z||000022||Racer 1||01-06-2001||12:53 AM||||When I was 15 I had just got a Kawasaki KE100. I passed the motorcycle driving school where the instructor told me I only had to have one leg down when I come to a complete stop. Then like 3 months later I pull up to a 4 way stop a cops right there also. I come to a complete stop and put one leg down like the inst said. THen the cop follows me and pulls me over. Gives me a ticket for not having <B>BOTH</B> feet down when I stopped. Then the cop told me he got the same ticket when he was my age for the exact same thing. Know tell what kinda BS is that? Now in my fiero I got pulled over once becuase the cop thought my fiero was a exoctic car but he didnt have any reason to pull me over. <P>For the people who get pulled over on a regular keep a box with glazed donuts in it and offer one to the officer as a ice breaker. <P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://spitfire.cwv.net/~cdbailey/images/gifssucl/eyes2/evil_eyes.gif"> ||||reg||13
Z||000023||loafer87gt||01-06-2001||01:21 AM||||I have never been bothered by the cops in my GT. I've only been pulled over twice in my life actually, back when I was young and stoopid. I kinda miss the officer we used to have policing our small town. 2 words to describe her: FAT AND WORTHLESS!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">Seriously, she is exactly like the cop off of SouthPark. We used to make her life a living hell back when I was in Highschool. One night I drove my Tercel through her lawn beside her house and clipped the fire hydrant with the drivers side. The next day she comes up and asks me and my buddies if we knew who might have done it, that a white vehicle drove though her yeard and left white paint on the hydrant. She failed to noticed the 2" scrape all the way across the drivers side of my car, so I told her that a bunch of guys from out of town were roaring around in a Ford Halftonne, in which she immediately went out looking for. Me and my older brother always used to have the East vs. West challenge with his Civic SI vs. my GT on the ride home from work. She was waiting at the intersection where the road to our town meets the highway, and I made the corner doing about 110 KPH with all four of my tires howling to beet jeezuz, failing to notice her car behind a sign. She must have been digging under the dash or something cause she failed to see me fly thru the corner, but the squeeling made her look up just in time to catch my brother do the same thing. Fiero=1 Civic=0||||reg||1
Z||000024||jerpro||01-06-2001||09:49 AM||||cpos, cops, cops...<BR>There are WAAY too many cops out there. <BR>Instead of dealing with stupid traffic tickets they sould be doing what their badge says "protect and serve"<BR>Cops should be dealing with delincuents, rapists, murderers and drug addicts. NOT a kid doing 10 over in his fiero!!!<BR>I live in Grand rapids mich. and I live right by a police station. I just hate seeing soo many cop cars!!! If they all average 2 tickets a day 7 days a week, that is 1246 tickets a week!!!! It is stupid and insane.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/mad.gif"><BR>I have been pulled over on my fiero a couple times, but it is usually in roads I don't know and it is usually because they lable me as an agressive driver.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"> <BR>but anyway, cops should be there to stop bullets and stop crime not to give out tickets.<BR><P>------------------<BR>Only try your best, and if you don't succeed... TRY HARDER.||||reg||1
Z||000025||StuGood||01-06-2001||02:11 PM||||I like most of the police officers.  A few of them could stand to take basic driving lessons, and set a better example for the rest of us, I suppose.  But for the most part, they are very courteous and <B>do</B> try to keep things from getting out of hand.  I try to return the favor.<P>One saturday morning, I was late to meet some friends to go fishing at Edmonds, WA.  I had slept in, so I scrambled out of bed, got ready and jumped into my rental car.  I zipped through a 15-mph jog in Kent, WA and was promptly greeted by a motorcycle cop's lights in my rearview.  I pulled off the road into a parking lot.<P>The officer was <B>not</B> happy.  "When I turn those lights on, you are supposed to <B>stop!</B>"  I told him I didn't want him to have to stop in the middle of the street.  He wanted to see my rental papers and license, which I gave him.  He was still pretty mad.  "From Kansas, huh?  Well, just so you know - we don't care where you're from, we can track you down, and we are <B>not</B> going to have you speeding through our fair city!"<P>It was just about daybreak.  I looked past the officer, at big hill behind him, with all the beautiful trees on it, showing their fall colors.  It was gorgeous.  I said, "<B>Fair</B> city?  I'd say it's at <B>least</B> good to excellent."<P>That did it.  The officer grinned, shook his head, tore up the ticket, and let me go with a "just take it easy."   I did.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">        ||||reg||6
Z||000026||Jackalrr||01-07-2001||02:55 PM||||The cops around where I live have been pretty nice so far. Couple weeks ago I was doing the speed limit (40) around a sharp turn into a parking lot on a wet road while it was raining, while racing, trying to cut through the parking lot and I slide sideways and almost ran right into a sheriff car. All he did was pull me over, check my license and tell me to slow down.<P>-Charlie<P>------------------<BR>--------<BR>jackalrr@cinci.rr.com<P>85 GT 5spd<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fieroperformance.com/mycar21.jpg">  <BR>http://www.FieroPerformance.com||||reg||10
Z||000027||My7Fieros||01-07-2001||03:03 PM||||<B>NO COMMENT!</B>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif">  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000028||Seanh||01-07-2001||05:40 PM||||I get in all kinds of trouble with my Fiero. I think the color of the car has alot to do with it to. I dont get pulled over in my silver car very much at all, maybe twice a year. Now, my black car, I would get pulled over atleast once a month. I have never got pulled over in my parents Lincolns, or Lexus, and I drive them just like I do in my car. I get alot of hell from cops with my Bronco too. They hate that thing because it could run them over without hesitation. I have never gotten questioned about drugs or alchohol, since I dont use either of them. The only time was in my Black Fiero, I cleaned the interior with a steam cleaner, and everything, after I was done, I sprayed it heavily with Fabreez to get rid of the smoke smell from the last owner and I got pulled over the next day. Cop started in asking me if the Fabreez was to get rid of the pot smell, told him my story and he droped it. ||||reg||1
Z||000029||StuGood||01-07-2001||06:00 PM||||Found it interesting what Seanh said.  I've been pulled over (and ticketed a couple times, deservedly so) in the Gold 1986 SE more often than any other car I've owned.  It's also been in more accidents (everything from parking lot scrapes to serious rear-enders), and quite a few near misses.  Seems nobody sees the car except the cops - maybe I'd better paint it some other color  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif">.<P>The Silver 1987 GT? Never been pulled over that I recall; definitely never ticketed.  The Black 1987 Cavalier- only pulled over once, for headlight out.  True, it's black, but it's no sports car.   ||||reg||1
